<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY13-QA-006>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY13-QA-006" ;
  triage:title "rust-best-practices RBP-F002: escalation-recipient fields in report.rs are raw Vec<String> instead of the AgentName newtype used elsewhere in the same structs" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1300-r1 (PR #1300, AY.13 doctor team scope). TeamEscalationRecipientsDoctorReport.recipients and EscalationRecipientsDoctorReport.daemon are typed Vec<String> even though these values are escalation-recipient agent identifiers; the surrounding doctor-report types in the same file (DoctorEnvironmentVisibility, DoctorExecutionContext) consistently use the existing AgentName/TeamName newtypes for the same kind of value. ax6.rs::daemon_recipients/team_recipients pull these strings from TaskStore::list_escalation_recipients/effective_escalation_recipients (both Result<Vec<String>, AtmError> in atm-storage) and pass them through unvalidated; the same raw Vec<String> shape is reused for real escalation dispatch in atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_escalation.rs. Secondary note: TeamEscalationRecipientsDoctorReport.source: String ('daemon default' / 'team' literals) is a two-value discriminant represented as a raw string; consider a small enum." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "type-safety" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/doctor/report.rs, crates/atm-core/src/doctor/ax6.rs, atm-storage::TaskStore, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_escalation.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
